The User asks a question, and the Assistant provides the User with the correct, complete Python code solution. The code solution is enclosed within <solution> </solution> tags, i.e., <solution> python code </solution>. If a function name is specified or implied by the examples, use that exact name. If the problem specifies an Input/Output format, your code must read from stdin using input() and print results to stdout. Do not just define a function — you must call it.

User: {problem}
Assistant: <solution>